- op: discuss  # 7008
  at: '2026-10-31T23:33:41Z'  # 7008
  by: agent  # 7008
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 7008
  clock: 2  # 7008
  nonce: '7008'  # 7008
  message: "Fix on local branch jgstern-agent/fix/zakij, commit e26e5a942b (not pushed; integration pending). Premise reproduced on a scratch fixture: <script context=\"module\" lang=\"ts\"> (Svelte) and <script type=\"module\" lang='ts'> (Vue) symbols came out language=javascript; worse than filed, a Vue <script setup generic=\"T extends Record<string, unknown>\" lang=\"ts\"> yielded NO symbols, because the old [^>]* tag tail stopped at the > inside the quoted generic and fed the rest of the tag to the parser. Fix: one quote-aware extractor (_extract_sfc_scripts) for both hosts; lang read by scanning whole attributes (order and quoting free; data-lang and lang= inside another quoted value do not count). ts/typescript -> TypeScript grammar, tsx -> TSX grammar (previously plain TS via the old regex's ts prefix, which misparses JSX), else JavaScript. Self-closing <script src=... /> is skipped instead of pairing with the next block's </script>. Tests: test_js_ts_sfc_script_lang.py (37 cases; 31 RED before; first-attribute-only mutant fails 19). Corpus scan (read-only regex over the 6710 .vue/.svelte files in whole_bunch_of_repos + curriculum_repos): 21 blocks change grammar (podman-desktop 19, workadventure 1, koel 1), plus vite playground/optimize-deps/generics.vue (generic with >). A/B on those dirs: e.g. podman-desktop Table.stories.svelte variable Person (JS misparse of a type alias) -> type Person; workadventure MessageInputBar.svelte gains the ApplicationProperty interface fields. Residual, not changed: a <script ...> spelled inside a JS string in a component (gitlab clone_code_dropdown.vue) is still taken as a block boundary, before and after."  # 7008
